==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|}}, from {{inh|de|goh|fliohan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*fleuhan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*fleuhaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vlieden}} and {{cog|en|flee}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈfliː.ən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-fliehen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|fliehen<floh,geflohen,flöhe.haben,sein>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive|auxiliary {{m|de|sein}}}} to [[flee]]; to [[escape]]
#: {{ux|de|Als die Polizei eintraf, war der Räuber bereits '''geflohen'''.|When the police arrived, the robber had already '''fled'''.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|auxiliary {{m|de|sein}}}} to [[diverge]] 
#: {{ux|de|Die Linien '''fliehen'''.|The lines diverge.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|auxiliary {{m|de|haben}}}} to [[flee]] from (someone); to [[avoid]] 
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''fliehe''' diesen Kerl wie die Pest.|I '''avoid''' that guy like the plague.}}

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj|fliehen<floh,geflohen,flöhe.haben,sein>}}

